s://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T19:33:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T19:33:24Z","body":"Does Godot have a bug bounty system or way to sponsor the fixing of this issue? I would like to ensure this problem gets solved.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573778359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573780773","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100890#issuecomment-2573780773","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100890","id":2573780773,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZaMcl","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T19:34:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T19:34:54Z","body":"Not really no, I will do some testing on this tomorrow and see if I can identify any specifics, but given the types I'm not sure it's a bug but a limitation on these types","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573780773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575668172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100890#issuecomment-2575668172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100890","id":2575668172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZhZPM","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T16:06:02Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T16:09:51Z","body":"Tested and the test setup is a bit blunt and doesn't handle things correctly as it doesn't actually check what shapes it hits or not (it just checks for *any* hits)\n\nBut for the `ConcavePolygonShape3D` the case is as I suggested, if you change any of the other shapes to *intersect* the concave shape instead of being strictly internal it works, as documented, so the case of the concave shape is as expected\n\nThis test needs to be reworked so it reliably tests interactions, so please clean the test up so each shape reliably tests against each other shape, this would require disabling or otherwise removing them, you also need to make sure it doesn't intersect *itself*\n\nThis could probably be achieved by using the physics layers (it might just be that you made an error in that by using the wrong layers, but not sure), so please update the MRP to handle this, as the current MRP isn't precise enough to do proper testing with\n\nEdit: Tweaked the layers and it now reports correctly, will test further later, but the change is this:\n```gdscript\nsubnode.collision_mask = 1\nsubnode.collision_layer = 1\nquery_parameters.collision_mask = 1\n\t\t\t\n#subnode.show()\n\t\t\t\n# Get the space state for collision checks\nvar space_state = subnode.get_world_3d().direct_space_state\n\t\t\t\n# Perform the shape collisComion check\nvar results = space_state.collide_shape(query_parameters)\n\t\t\t\nif results.size() == 0: #No Collisions?\n\tprint(\"Checking if \" + shapeNode.name + \" can hit the \" + subnode.name + \". It can't.\")\nelse:\n\tprint(\"Checking if \" + shapeNode.name + \" can hit the \" + subnode.name + \" It can.\")\n\t\t\t\nsubnode.collision_mask = 0\nsubnode.collision_layer = 0\n```\nAnd clearing the layer and mask for all the bodies in the scene","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575668172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575694648","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100890#issuecomment-2575694648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100890","id":2575694648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zhfs4","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T16:15:37Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T16:15:37Z","body":"So to summarize what I found:\n* Concave shapes work as documented, they only intersect on the boundary\n* The separation shape is a question though, needs evaluating, I think it doesn't support collision, only other interaction like forces\n\nSo this needs to be worked out, but the separation shape is the part that's uncertain, and likely just needs to be documented ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575694648/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575735011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100890#issuecomment-2575735011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100890","id":2575735011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zhpjj","user":{"login":"CaveManon","id":67725455,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NDU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67725455?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon","html_url":"https://github.com/CaveManon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaveManon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T16:30:14Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T16:30:14Z","body":">But for the ConcavePolygonShape3D the case is as I suggested, if you change any of the other shapes to intersect the concave shape instead of being strictly internal it works, as documented, so the case of the concave shape is as expected\n\nThis was the issue we had, but if it's documented then its an error on our development team's part. Our solution for the issue we were having in our actual code base was to shape cast a WorldBoundary3D towards a Concave Shape to get our desired results rather than the other way around. For some reason that fixed our code.\n\nOn another note, where is the documentation for this found? The best I could find was this:\n> Warning: Physics bodies that are small have a chance to clip through this shape when moving fast. This happens because on one frame, the physics body may be on the \"outside\" of the shape, and on the next frame it may be \"inside\" it. ConcavePolygonShape3D is hollow, so it won't detect a collision.\n\nThis does explain the functionality but is easy to skip over since it talks about moving objects and speed rather than emphasizing that these are hollow. Putting the hollowness as a note first and then the example with the speed second would be useful for developers in the future.\n\n>Tweaked the layers and it now reports correctly, will test further later, but the change is this:\nI'm currently updating the MRP with this functionality.\n\n\nWould you like that I rename this issue to reflect your summary? I'm going to go ahead and edit the issue's description again to make note about Concave polygons having expected functionality.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575735011/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575761332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100890#issuecomment-2575761332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100890","id":2575761332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zhv-0","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T16:41:36Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T17:02:51Z","body":"It's right there (but could be made a little bit more clear):\n> However, `ConcavePolygonShape3D` is hollow even if the interconnected triangles do enclose a volume, which often makes it unsuitable for physics or detection.\n\nYes let's focus this on investigating the separation shape, and then document it if this is intended, or discuss how to improve it otherwise","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575761332/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807189700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100890#issuecomment-2807189700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100890","id":2807189700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nUlDE","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T18:57:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T18:57:35Z","body":"It looks like the behaviour of SeparationRayShape3D is still the same as of `v4.5.dev.custom_build [215acd52e]`. It also seems like whether or not this was intentional was not established. Based on the docs for 4.4 ([link](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/classes/class_separationrayshape3d.html)), this shape has special functionality to move itself and so its divergence in behaviourmay be a natural result of this.\n\ncc @AThousandShips ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807189700/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]